# How to build on this codebase

Read `CLAUDE.md` for full tables (actions, NPCs, milestones, CSS tokens, DOM IDs).

| Task | Where to edit |
|------|----------------|
| Action duration, cost, reward | `data/actions.json` (see `data/README.md`) |
| Day length, faith regen, payday | `data/timing.json` |
| New action | `data/actions.json` + `ACTION_UNLOCK` in `js/actions.js` + `ACTION_TEXT` in `js/language.js` |
| New location | `js/locations.js` + bg class in `css/style.css` |
| New NPC | `js/npcs.js` + default in `js/state.js` |
| New milestone | `js/milestones.js` |
| UI / layout | `index.html` + `js/ui.js` |
| Save key / format | `js/save.js` (bump key if breaking saves) |
| BGM | `js/audio.js` |
| Location art | `background-image` on `.location-bg` |

**Design constraints:** One action at a time; costs at start, rewards at end; cancel refunds half faith cost; auto-save every 30 engine ticks + on action complete; no offline progress.

**Locked actions — always show why:** Any gated action must list every requirement on its card with current progress (✓ done / ○ missing + “Now: …”). Implement in `getActionRequirements()` + `REQUIREMENT_BUILDERS` in `js/actions.js` and render via `action-requirements` in `js/ui.js`. Do not rely on `unlockHint` alone or hide requirements when locked.

**Japan authenticity:** Preserve onsen, English events, station tracts, slow trust arcs, monthly support, shame/wa in stage gates — see `CLAUDE.md` § Authentic Japan touches.
